null,"degas_padj":null},{"cell_type":"Ex","gene_symbol":"CD24","gene_symbol_current":"CD24","gene_id":"ENSG00000272398","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":1.82398e-56,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.151132,"nucleus_score":-15.8998,"pct_ad":0.0841184,"pct_control":0.102818,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.808495,"donor_log2fc":0.185928,"donor_lfcse":0.253669,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":0.00261248,"degas_log2fc":0.131637,"degas_padj":2.22025e-09},{"cell_type":"In","gene_symbol":"CD24","gene_symbol_current":"CD24","gene_id":"ENSG00000272398","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.977314,"donor_log2fc":-0.0227786,"donor_lfcse":0.177378,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.000337328,"degas_log2fc":null,"degas_padj":null}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"In","gene_id":"ENSG00000272398","module":"blue","kme":0.193908,"hub":false,"module_direction":"lower in AD","module_padj":0.137528,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000272398","entrez_id":["100133941"],"uniprot":["P25063"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a sialoglycoprotein that is expressed on mature granulocytes and B cells and modulates growth and differentiation signals to these cells. The precursor protein is cleaved to a short 32 amino acid mature peptide which is anchored via a glycosyl phosphatidylinositol (GPI) link to the cell surface. This gene was missing from previous genome assemblies, but is properly located on chromosome 6. Non-transcribed pseudogenes have been designated on chromosomes 1, 15, 20, and Y. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants. [provided by RefSeq, Apr 2014].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"P25063","text":"May have a pivotal role in cell differentiation of different cell types. Signaling could be triggered by the binding of a lectin-like ligand to the CD24 carbohydrates, and transduced by the release of second messengers derived from the GPI-anchor. Modulates B-cell activation responses. Promotes AG-dependent proliferation of B-cells, and prevents their terminal differentiation into antibody-forming cells (PubMed:11313396). In association with SIGLEC10 may be involved in the selective suppression of the immune response to danger-associated molecular patterns (DAMPs) such as HMGB1, HSP70 and HSP90. Plays a role in the control of autoimmunity (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}